+#
+# At T <= DL2_MAX_TOKENS (config only; its own bound, not DL_MAX_TOKENS), with the stage-1 chain ON and
+# the prepare() self-check passed (state["dl2_ok"]), two more kernels from the P body replace the
+# attention side's nvjet GEMMs and small nodes:
+#   Q dl_qkv_kernel: qkv_gate GEMV (36 head tiles x 6 K-splits = 216 CTAs) whose last-ticket CTA per tile
+#     does FusedQKNorm (scaleless RMSNorm eps RMS_EPS, interleaved RoPE from state["cos_sin"]), the k/v
+#     divide when kv_scale != 1, the E4M3 casts (via bf16), the cache store at cache_loc and the q cast /
+#     paired zero-padded [T,16,128] write. Replaces the qkv GEMM + splitK reduce, qk_norm, k/v divide, both
+#     .to(FP8), store_cache and the q cast or pad copies.
+#   O dl_o_kernel: o GEMV (128 row tiles x 2 K-halves = 256 CTAs, the weight slab resident in smem) whose
+#     prologue does the per-head RMSNorm x sigmoid(gate) of FA3's output (unpaired or paired, taking each
+#     head's own half), replacing the unpad copies, o_norm_gate and the o GEMM. FA3 is unchanged and
+#     attends every key.
+# Adversarial-review carve-out (a): at sliding decode_1 (window, B=1, L=1) master's _sliding_forward owns
+# the attention chain, so DL2_SLIDING1 = "raw" runs Q in raw mode (bf16 qkv [T, 2304] for _sliding_forward)
+# and O without the prologue (its input is already normed and gated); "nvjet" keeps master's GEMMs there.
+# Both are config-only and logged.
